# .rabadon/ holds two different things: live per-machine session state, and the
# guard this repo enforces on ITSELF. Ignoring the directory hid both, so
# guard_lint_test.sh's "this repo's own guard.json lints clean" arm passed here
# and died in every clean clone. Ignore the contents, re-include only the guard.
# `.rabadon/` (whole directory) would make the negation a no-op: git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so a file inside cannot be un-ignored.
# The glob must stay `**/.rabadon/*`, not `.rabadon/*`: a pattern with a slash
# in it anchors to this file's directory, which would un-ignore the nested
# native/.rabadon, site/.rabadon and reports/*/.rabadon — each of which holds
# its own state.json/handoff.md. The negation IS anchored, on purpose: only the
# root guard is shipped, nested ones stay local.
**/.rabadon/*
!/.rabadon/guard.json
# built binaries — the source is the artifact, not the a.out. Every
# rabadon-<name> executable, never the .cpp/.h/.sh that make them.
native/rabadon-*
!native/rabadon-*.cpp
!native/rabadon-*.h
!native/rabadon-*.sh
*.o

# platform packages carry binaries only in CI (copied in before publish),
# never committed — the package.json/README templates ARE committed.
npm/*/rabadon-*

# npm pack output
*.tgz

# the micro benchmark is a built binary like the rest; the source is the artifact
native/gate_bench
